CRE oracle capital-flow snapshots
├── when a snapshot precedes or follows a withdrawal
│   ├── the 1000 minus 150 example yields 850 in both cases
│   ├── withdrawing everything leaves zero rather than restoring stale assets
│   └── allocations and withdrawals after a snapshot are applied exactly once
├── when checking movement limits
│   ├── compare NAV with the historical flow-adjusted baseline
│   └── requests and post-snapshot withdrawals do not become investment gains or losses
├── when reconciling signed accounting
│   ├── realized profits allow cumulative net capital to become negative
│   ├── negative historical or current NAV cannot be approved by guard review
│   └── signed overflow, underflow and out-of-range reports never wrap into valid NAV
└── when authenticating a rejected snapshot
    ├── preserve the exact five-word payload for review
    └── applying the reviewed snapshot includes all intervening capital flows
